495,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**Summary:**\r\n\r\nWhen a test class fixture implements both IAsyncLifetime and IDisposable, corresponding Dispose methods are executed in parallel despite the documentation:\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\n     /// <summary>\r\n    /// Called when an object is no longer needed. Called just before <see cref=\"M:System.IDisposable.Dispose\" />\r\n    /// if the class also implements that.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    Task DisposeAsync();\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Source:**\r\nhttps://github.com/xunit/xunit/blob/1fb6b672768bed98f5e7b6656c1bbb3792ed0530/src/xunit.execution/Sdk/Frameworks/Runners/XunitTestClassRunner.cs#L156-L164\r\n\r\n**Workaround**\r\nJust use one or another interface\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is the same bug as https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/1749 but for `XunitTestClassRunner`","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/1772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/1772/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]